eeper who's retelling of a recent  event doesn't seem quite right she's  quick to point out that he seems Shady a  lawyer is smart and resourceful a fact  that her friends never failed to remind  her of but she also struggles to make  connections and masks her discomfort in  engaging with people with sarcasm and  spaz I've heard a lot of my friends say  that a boy talks too much is too  judgmental too sassy or spends too much  time bitching about the weather but you  know who else spends a lot of time  bitching about the weather you do or at  least I do it's a simple touch that I  think makes a law a whole lot more  relatable if you've been bullied or know  what it's like to be on the outside of  social groups looking in I'm betting  you'll understand her standoffish and  guarded tendencies turf when alloy does  begin to open up it's really  heartwarming you can see other  characters earning her trust you watch  friendships form you feel her genuine  pain when she empathizes with an NPC  over a tragic situation like the loss of  a family member a lot of that is due to  Ashley birches excellent voice work but  Ayla is also just an exceptionally  well-written character she's not afraid  to pull someone up for flirting with her  or disrespecting her for being a woman  or Nora hey Louise confidence rarely  wavers and she doesn't take [ __ ] and  that's exactly the kind of character you  want to be playing when you have to  fight menacing towering machines alloy  is consistently tough and independent  and what she learns on her travels is  the importance of letting people help  her and trusting people enough to be  part of a community again after  finishing horizon you might feel like I  do I spent about 50 hours with a Lloyd  getting to know her and eventually  closing the book on her story and I miss  her and that's awesome  you  [Music]
 

